  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Multiplying Binomials</title>
<para>Write an expression equivalent to \((x + 2)(x + 5)\).</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Distribute. Use FOIL. Multiply the First terms, Outer terms, Inner terms, and Last terms.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="DIAGRAM SHOWING X PLUS 2 TIMES X PLUS 5. ON THE TOP, IN RED, AN ARROW IS GOING FROM X TO X. ANOTHER ARROW IS GOING FROM X TO 5. ON THE BOTTOM, IN BLUE, AN ARROW IS GOING FROM 2 TO X. ANOTHER ARROW IS GOING FROM 2 TO 5."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/3822dad5581e1732013f18f666bb03845bc4a2aa"/></media></figure></para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Write out the four terms.
  \(x^2+5x+2x+10\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Combine like terms.
  \(x^2+7x+10\)</para>
<title>Try It: Multiplying Binomials</title>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Write an expression equivalent to \((x + 7)(x + 3)\).</para>
  <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Here is how to multiply binomial expressions:</para>
  <para><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Distribute.</para>
  <para><figure><media alt="DIAGRAM SHOWING X PLUS 7 TIMES X PLUS 3. ON THE TOP, IN RED, AN ARROW IS GOING FROM X TO X. ANOTHER ARROW IS GOING FROM X TO 3. ON THE BOTTOM, IN BLUE, AN ARROW IS GOING FROM 7 TO X. ANOTHER ARROW IS GOING FROM 7 TO 3."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/883809925e586f9a5248a4f608762735d1535f2c"/></media></figure></para>
  <para><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Write out the four terms.
    \(x^2+3x+7x+10\)</para>
  <para><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Combine like terms.
    \(x^2+10x+21\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
</content>
